  "critical_findings": [
    "Rather2014 uses V_pinu=1.2 MeV in 104Pd, transferred from Cd, not a larger separately measured four-hole value; jnu=16, n=8, Jcoupling=5, Jrot=17.",
    "Roy2011 uses V_pinu=1.2 MeV in 106,108,110Cd; it varies effective jnu (18,16,10), n, and core response, not a measured monotone V(N).",
    "Four g9/2 holes do not imply twice the quadrupole torque: exact axial paired-hole controls give Qh=-72 for 2holes |m|=9/2, -96 for 4holes |m|=9/2,7/2, but -24 for 4holes |m|=9/2,1/2.",
    "For Jcore=0 the fixed-blade B(E2)(I) curve is independent of V_pinu; V changes frequency/torque. For positive stable core response larger V or core inertia can slow closure per unit spin.",
    "A quadratic core-response derivation yields induced Qpi^T Fpi^T C^-1 Fnu Qnu coupling; core quadrupole softness and rotational inertia are different response functions.",
    "N does not uniquely fix h11/2 occupation: gd mixing, pairing and rotational crossings matter. No full even-even 102-108Pd AMR parameter chain exists in the reviewed evidence."
  ],
